summary:
  The tag list is the one "Show more" pages only when the web list holds rows.

history:
  Whether the tag answer's list or the name answer's was paged was told by
  the web rows the tag answer had put in. The listener's own stations are
  left out of those, so under "jazz" a tag page of fifty saved stations put
  none in and paging stayed with the name answer, an empty one: the genre's
  fifty-first station could not be reached. The search now asks
  SearchLogic.tagListPaged, which reads the two answers.

target:
  package/contents/ui/FullRepresentation.qml

find:
                      if (tagOk && SearchLogic.tagListPaged(lead !== null, fullRepresentation._webPage.more, tagRows, tagPage.more))

replace:
                      if (tagOk && webResultsModel.count > 0 && SearchLogic.tagListPaged(lead !== null, fullRepresentation._webPage.more, tagRows, tagPage.more))

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_the_list_show_more_pages_is_read_from_the_two_answers.
  Line-neutral.
